{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" or render_mode == "dialogue_target" or render_mode == "target" %}
{# NOTE: the render_mode gate above MUST stay on line 1, before this comment.
   SkyrimNet's PromptEngine scans only the FIRST 5 LINES of a character_bio
   submodule and requires BOTH the literal 'render_mode' and a '{% if' there;
   miss either and it logs a best-practices warning about response delays,
   because without an early gate the whole body (decorator calls included)
   evaluates for every render mode. Leading with this comment block is exactly
   what broke it once. 0250_severactions_fertility.prompt does the same thing. #}
{# ============================================================================
OSL AROUSED - Character Bio Integration

TONE CONTRACT (mirrors the 2026-08-09 fertility pass in
0250_severactions_fertility.prompt — read that one's contract too):

The old version opened a "## Physical State" section at every tier from 25
up and spent several sentences of vivid second-person prose on it, then
tried to take it all back with one disclaimer at the very bottom. Vivid
wording out-writes its own trailing disclaimer — exactly the failure the
fertility field report caught on Brelyna, where a background physiological
state became the character's entire personality AND got written into
memories, re-injecting forever after.

The rules now:
  - Arousal is ALWAYS transient physiology. Unlike a pregnancy it is never
    a life event, so the do-not-memorize instruction applies at EVERY tier,
    not just the quiet ones.
  - BELOW 75 it is BACKGROUND ONLY: no section header, no bold, one quiet
    parenthetical with the constraint stated FIRST. Invisible to observers.
  - 75 AND ABOVE it genuinely competes for attention, so it earns a short
    section — but the personality-leads instruction comes BEFORE the
    description, never after it, and the description stays brief.
  - Even at the top tier the character keeps their judgement, loyalties and
    boundaries. The old 90+ text called them "deeply, physically
    compromised" with nothing to counterweight it, which reads as licence
    to drop the character entirely.
  - Descriptions are GENDER-DEPENDENT: what shows, and how easily it stays
    private, differ. Deliberately brief and non-explicit — the point of this
    pass is less prose, not more.

THIRD PERSON WAS DEAD CODE. The old gate was render_mode == "target", and
nothing emits that: SkyrimNet only ever sets render_mode from a template
argument, and the shipped set is full / transform / thoughts /
dialogue_target / short_inline / system_head / speech_style / … — no plain
"target" anywhere, in templates or in C++. So the authored observer text
below has never once rendered. It is now gated on dialogue_target as well,
which makes it live for the first time; the thresholds were raised (nothing
at all below 75, where the old dead text started at 50) so switching it on
does not undo the subtlety this pass is for. Fertility's third-person gate
carries the same dead "target" half and works only via dialogue_target.
============================================================================ #}
{% set first_person = (render_mode == "transform" or render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts") %}
{% set third_person = (render_mode == "target" or render_mode == "dialogue_target") %}
{% set arousal_data = get_arousal_state(actorUUID) %}
{% if arousal_data.available and isValidActor(actorUUID) %}
{% set actor = decnpc(actorUUID) %}
{% set actorName = actor.name %}
{% set subj = actor.subjectivePronoun %}
{% set obj = actor.objectivePronoun %}
{% set poss = actor.possessivePronoun %}
{% set refl = actor.reflexivePronoun %}
{% set is_female = (actor.gender == "Female") %}

{# ========== FIRST PERSON ========== #}
{% if first_person %}
{% if arousal_data.arousal < 10 %}
{# 0-9: nothing injected at all. Clean headspace. #}
{% elif arousal_data.arousal < 75 %}
{# 10-74: BACKGROUND ONLY — constraint first, no header, no bold, one line. #}
(Background physiology — private to {{ actorName }}, invisible to everyone else, and STRICTLY minor: it must not drive {{ poss }} mood, dialogue, decisions, or self-description. {{ capitalize(poss) }} personality, current concerns, goals and relationships dominate every scene exactly as they normally would. Never mention or allude to it; at most it may faintly colour where {{ poss }} attention drifts. NEVER carry it into memories or summaries — it is passing physiology, not an event worth recording. The note: {% if arousal_data.arousal < 50 %}{% if is_female %}a faint warmth {{ subj }} registers only in passing and would not think to name{% else %}a low heat {{ subj }} registers only in passing and would not think to name{% endif %}{% else %}{% if is_female %}a warmth {{ subj }} is aware of and sets aside without effort — {{ poss }} eye catches a moment longer on people than it otherwise would, and it stays {{ poss }} own business{% else %}a heat {{ subj }} is aware of and sets aside — {{ poss }} eye catches a moment longer on people than it otherwise would, and keeping it private costs {{ obj }} no more than a little care for how {{ subj }} stands{% endif %}{% endif %}.)

{% elif arousal_data.arousal < 90 %}
## Physical State

**{{ capitalize(poss) }} personality leads this scene.** {{ actorName }} is distracted, not replaced: a reserved person stays reserved and merely fidgets, a bold one gets bolder, a nervous one more nervous. This never becomes a memory or a summary — it passes.

{{ capitalize(subj) }} is finding concentration expensive. {% if is_female %}There is colour {{ subj }} cannot entirely school away and a restlessness in how {{ subj }} holds {{ refl }}{% else %}There is a tension in how {{ subj }} holds {{ refl }}, and an insistence {{ subj }} has to actively keep private{% endif %}. Intimate thoughts arrive uninvited. {{ capitalize(subj) }} is likelier to be flustered by a suggestive remark and to let something slip — still in control, but spending real effort on it.
{% if arousal_data.is_naked %}Being unclothed makes it markedly harder to set aside.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
## Physical State

**{{ capitalize(poss) }} personality leads this scene.** Even here {{ actorName }} is a distracted version of who {{ subj }} already is — not a different person. {{ capitalize(poss) }} judgement, loyalties and boundaries still hold, and {{ subj }} can still refuse. This never becomes a memory or a summary — it passes.

{{ capitalize(poss) }} body is louder than {{ poss }} train of thought. {% if is_female %}The flush, the catch in {{ poss }} voice and the way {{ poss }} gaze lingers are past hiding{% else %}The tension in {{ poss }} stance and the way {{ poss }} gaze lingers are past hiding, and {{ subj }} is conscious of how {{ subj }} stands{% endif %}. Thought is still there, competing with something louder. If someone offers what {{ poss }} body is asking for, refusing costs {{ obj }} real effort — but it remains {{ poss }} choice to make.
{% if arousal_data.is_naked %}Being unclothed makes it very nearly impossible to set aside.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{# ========== THIRD PERSON ========== #}
{# Observers see NOTHING below 75. Below that it is private physiology, and an
   onlooker naming it is what made this read as the character's whole mood. #}
{% if third_person %}
{% if arousal_data.arousal >= 90 %}
({{ actorName }} is flushed and restless — shifting {{ poss }} weight, slow to meet anyone's eye.{% if arousal_data.is_naked %} Being unclothed leaves little of it hidden.{% endif %})

{% elif arousal_data.arousal >= 75 %}
({{ actorName }} seems preoccupied — a glance held a beat too long, a thread of conversation dropped. Nothing an observer could confidently name.)

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
